Article 131
Promotive efforts as referred to in Article 130 are carried out by providing socialization or counseling to the community regarding healthy lifestyle patterns which include a. the importance of exclusive breastfeeding for infants;
the importance of immunization for toddlers;
clean living patterns;
the importance of nutritious food; and the dangers of drugs and smoking.

Article 53
Integrated services for women victims of violence as referred to in Article 52 shall be implemented by upholding principles, which include:
a. gender responsive;
b. non-discrimination;
c. equal and respectful relationships;
d. maintaining confidentiality;
e. providing a sense of security and comfort;
-31- respecting individual differences;
f. non-judgmental;
g. respecting the choices and decisions of victims;
h. sensitive to the background and conditions of victims and
i. use of language that is appropriate and understood by victims;
j. fast and simple;
k. empathy; and
l. fulfillment of women's rights.

Article 48
Empowerment of women victims of violence as referred to in Article 47 may take the form of:
a. job skills training;
b. development of productive economic enterprises both individual and group;
c. capital assistance by facilitating soft loans; d. facilitating access to the banking and non-banking sectors; and
e. marketing assistance for various products produced by women victims of violence.

