Article 44
Regional Government in the effort to protect Women as referred to in Article 42 is responsible for carrying out the following matters:
a. planning, making, establishing and implementing policies, programs and activities for the protection of Women;
b. strengthening and developing institutions providing Women protection services;
c. early on carrying out various preventive efforts so that violence against Women does not occur or can be minimized;
d. massively and continuously carrying out various efforts so that acts of violence against Women do not occur in all fields of life;
e. massively and continuously preventing the occurrence of TPPO; and
f. continuously striving to provide protection for Women workers.

Article 23
In order to implement the objective of providing protection for Women's rights from various forms of violence and other discriminatory treatment as referred to in Article 20 letter, it shall be carried out through:
a. promotive efforts;
b. preventive efforts;
c. curative efforts; and
d. rehabilitative efforts, in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 198
Every parent who in their home has a Woman, has a role in the following matters:
a. providing equal and comparable opportunities to Women in terms of obtaining access and opportunities to undergo education at all levels;
b. preventing every Woman who is part of the family members under their leadership from receiving arbitrary, harsh, and inhumane treatment; protecting their family members who are Women so that they do not experience pressure and sexual harassment, physical and psychological violence that causes the Woman concerned to be unable to live her life properly;
c. preventing a family member who is a Woman from entering into early marriage below the age limit determined by Law; and not forcing a Woman family member to marry a man/male whom she does not desire.

